---
/**
 * ACADEMICS · BOARD RESULTS — audit A1.
 *
 * ⚠ THIS PAGE EXISTS BECAUSE THE ALTERNATIVE WAS WORSE, NOT TO FILL A SUBMENU.
 * The route was already in the navigation and referenced from careerTopics, and
 * it was rendering the site's generic "We're still writing this page"
 * placeholder. For the single most-searched fact about any CBSE school, that
 * reads as an unfinished website rather than as an unpublished number — and it
 * sends the reader away with nothing. A specific answer, even a negative one,
 * is worth more than a generic one.
 *
 * ⚠ NO RESULT IS ESTIMATED, INFERRED OR ILLUSTRATED. docs/01 § 3.8 records
 * board results as: "no pass %, no toppers, no year-on-year data". The client
 * brief asked for a "98% Board Results" counter. It is not here and must never
 * be: a school's results are the one number a family will act on, and an invented
 * one would be indistinguishable from a measured one.
 *
 * ═══ WHAT THE SCHOOL DOES PUBLISH ABOUT OUTCOMES ═══════════════════════════
 * Discovered during the Section E rebuild, and the reason this page is three
 * sections rather than one:
 *   CUET (UG) 2025 — result cards per student, with NTA scores and subject
 *     percentiles, across PCM, Commerce and Humanities.
 *   "Vision To Reality" placement board, session 2024-25 — eighteen named
 *     leavers with course and institution; ten at University of Delhi colleges,
 *     three at BHU.
 * Neither is a board result. Both are outcomes, and a parent who came here for
 * evidence of where students end up should not leave empty-handed.
 *
 * Composition: statement (sand — the gap, stated at poster size) → split (paper,
 * photo LEFT — what IS published) → close.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import AcStatement from '../../components/academics/system/AcStatement.astro';
import AcSplit from '../../components/academics/system/AcSplit.astro';
import AcClose from '../../components/academics/system/AcClose.astro';

import banner from '../../assets/library/DSC_1226 copy.jpg';
import pLib from '../../assets/photos/sb-library.jpg';
import pBench from '../../assets/photos/sb-chem-lab.jpg';
import pCohort from '../../assets/photos/sunbeem-5.jpg';

const school = 'Sunbeam School Ballia';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Board Results — Sunbeam School Ballia"
  description="Sunbeam School Ballia does not publish its CBSE Class X and XII board results. This page says so plainly, and sets out the outcome data the school does publish — CUET scores and named university placements."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Board Results"
    standfirst="The school has not published them. This page says that rather than estimating a number you would plan around."
    crumbs={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Academics', href: '/academics/' },
    ]}
    src={banner}
    alt="The Nalanda Library at Sunbeam School Ballia, its shelves signed by subject."
    position="50% 48%"
  />

  <div class="u-page-panel ac-panel">
    <AcStatement
      ground="sand"
      ghost="%"
      ghostAt="right"
      texture={true}
      kicker="What is published"
      statement="No pass rate.<br /><em>No toppers.</em>"
      body={[
        'Sunbeam School Ballia does not currently publish its <strong>CBSE Class X and Class XII results</strong> — no pass percentage, no toppers, and no year-on-year data. That is the whole of the position, and it is stated here rather than worked around.',
        'It would be easy to fill this page. A pass percentage is the most expected number on a school website, and almost nobody checks one. That is exactly why it is not here: a figure invented on this page would be indistinguishable from a figure the school had measured, and a family would choose a school on it.',
        'When the school supplies its results, they belong here — with the year, the cohort size and the board attached, so they can be read rather than trusted.',
      ]}
    />

    <AcSplit
      ground="paper"
      side="left"
      ratio="wide"
      aspect="3 / 2"
      kicker="But the search does not have to end here"
      heading="What the school<br /><em>does publish</em>"
      body={[
        'A parent looking for board results is really asking a broader question: <em>where do students here end up?</em> On that, the school publishes more than most schools in the district — just not in the form of a percentage.',
        'It publishes <strong>CUET (UG) 2025 results card by card</strong>, with the NTA score and every subject percentile, across PCM, Commerce and Humanities. And it prints a placement board, <strong>“Vision To Reality”</strong>, naming <strong>eighteen leavers of session 2024-25 with their course and institution</strong> — ten of them at University of Delhi colleges and three at Banaras Hindu University.',
        'Neither is a board result, and neither is presented as one. Both are set out in full on <strong>University Counselling</strong>.',
      ]}
      photo={pLib}
      alt={`Students of ${school} reading at the long tables of the Nalanda Library, a member of staff at the head of the row`}
      inset={pBench}
      insetAlt={`Students of ${school} working along the chemistry bench, test tubes held over the burners`}
    />

    <AcClose
      owed={true}
      statement="Unpublished,<br /><em>not unmeasured.</em>"
      body="The school holds its board results; it has simply not published them. Until it does, this site will not print a figure — the office below can answer for a particular year, and the outcome data that is published sits on University Counselling."
      photo={pCohort}
      alt={`Student council office-bearers and NCC cadets of ${school} on stage with the school’s dignitaries`}
      position="50% 38%"
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  div.ac-panel { padding-block: 0; }
</style>
